# pins.env -- every version pin this environment carries.
#
# Two groups, one file, because both are ENVIRONMENT policy and both are
# read from this same directory:
#
#   * the FLEET executables (clai, ast-mcp, gadmin, git-mirror), read by the
#     vendored acquire engine as its sibling -- acquire.sh derives
#     ACQUIRE_FLEET_PINS from its own directory;
#   * sandbox-qol, the one tool this package installs OUTSIDE the acquire
#     rail, read by setup-core.sh's load_pins.
#
# The fleet group used to ride inside the published
# @nine-at-a-time-media/skills payload (D1). That coupled executable version
# policy to the skills SOURCE, so when skills moved to their own repository
# (9atatimer/Skills) clai's version policy would have gone with them. The
# skills package is the source of truth for skills and nothing else; the
# lmde/clai environment stays in the tooling repos. D1's actual goal -- that
# a pin bump reach every surface on its next session rather than freezing
# into an environment snapshot -- still holds: this file ships in
# @nine-at-a-time-media/sandbox, and the session-start engine reruns acquire
# every session against the version it carries.
#
# Byte-identical twin: template-tools packages/naatm-sandbox/lib/pins.env. The same D2 discipline
# that governs acquire.sh's two copies governs this file's two copies.
#
# The review gate is unchanged: bumping a pin is a reviewed PR (ai-tools#72
# -- a default-branch push never grants execution in consumers).
#
# Resolution order per fleet package: explicit --pins argument > this file >
# float to registry latest. Plain KEY="value" only -- no logic, no command
# substitution. An absent or UNSET key floats that package.

# --- Fleet executables (acquire rail) ---

# clai. 0.9.0 is the first release that RUNS ON macOS: every earlier version,
# 0.8.0 included, bundled the OTLP gRPC exporter, whose `grpcio` native
# extension is compiled for the build host (ubuntu-latest), so clai died at
# import with `ImportError: ... cygrpc` anywhere else (#522, fixed by #523).
# Cloud sandboxes are Linux and never saw it; laptops could not start clai at
# all. Do NOT pin back below 0.9.0.
#
# 0.9.0 is also the first release with no bundled clai/_data fallback (#520):
# clai resolves the payload only from CLAI_DATA_DIR or the acquired package,
# and reports BOOTSTRAP_REQUIRED when neither is present.
CLAI_VERSION="0.9.0"

# ast-mcp. The AST MCP server, installed at ~/.local/bin/ast-mcp.
AST_MCP_VERSION="0.4.0"

# gadmin (@nine-at-a-time-media/admin -- npm name `admin`, binary `gadmin`).
ADMIN_VERSION="0.4.0"

# git-mirror: NOT PUBLISHED to GitHub Packages as of 2026-08-13 (npm view
# fails). UNSET floats it, which degrades fail-open with a warning until it
# is published (tds-utils#188).
GIT_MIRROR_VERSION="UNSET"

# There is deliberately NO SKILLS_VERSION key. The engine never applied this
# file to the skills row -- pinning the payload from a pins file the payload
# used to contain was a self-reference -- and skills float by design: a skill
# merge in 9atatimer/Skills IS the rollout. For an emergency skills freeze,
# pass an explicit --pins file with SKILLS_VERSION set.

# --- Outside the acquire rail ---

# The quality-of-life seeder, installed at user scope alongside the fleet.
# The session-start hook invokes it per-repo (create-if-absent) to drop
# defaults like .github/pull_request_template.md into the session's
# checkout. NOTE: not yet published to GitHub Packages as of 2026-08-13
# (npm view fails); until it is, this install degrades fail-open every
# build.
SANDBOX_QOL_VERSION="0.1.0"
